&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Figma is growing our team of passionate creatives and builders on a mission to make design accessible to all. Figma’s platform helps teams bring ideas to life—whether you&#39;re brainstorming, creating a prototype, translating designs into code, or iterating with AI. From idea to product, Figma empowers teams to streamline workflows, move faster, and work together in real time from anywhere in the world. If you&#39;re excited to shape the future of design and collaboration, join us!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Figma is building its founding Forward Deployed Engineering team to solve the complex, real-world challenges that emerge when bringing Figma’s products into large-scale enterprise environments and looking for founding Forward Deployed Engineers. As a Forward Deployed Engineer, you’ll embed directly with strategic customers, working across their codebases, design systems, developer environments, and workflows to make Figma’s products successful within their unique technical constraints. You’ll tackle the hardest adoption challenges hands-on, from complex frontend stacks and legacy systems to security and access requirements, while building trusted partnerships with customers’ senior engineering teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a senior/staff-level engineering role within Product and Engineering, not a sales or services function. You’ll work directly in customer environments when needed, using the minimum access required. Your goal is smooth adoption by the customer’s product and engineering teams, which means making complex workflows work simply in their environment and solving the underlying problems You’ll do that hands-on, often by writing Figma product code, then turn what you learn into a reusable path for future customers instead of taking permanent ownership of the customer’s codebase. Working closely with Figma’s Product, Engineering, Sales, and Customer Experience teams, you’ll help shape both the product and how this brand-new function works and scales. The role is highly collaborative, deeply customer-facing, and built for engineers who thrive in ambiguity, take end-to-end ownership, and want to solve the highest-impact problems at the intersection of product, engineering, and customer needs. This role includes periodic travel to work alongside strategic customers in person.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a full time role that can be held from one of our US hubs or remotely in the United States.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;What you&#39;ll do at Figma:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make an enterprise design system agent-ready so AI tools generate faithful, on-system code: fix tokens, naming, and guidelines, wire up Code Connect, and run evals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Get Make Local, Code Layers, and our newest products working in a customer’s real environment, writing code, config, agent skills, and guideline files against their systems and ours&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run technical discovery: understand a customer&#39;s dev environment, toolchain, and constraints, then scope the fastest credible path to value, in addition to setting the customer up for long term success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Debug hard, unfamiliar integration problems (git workflows, CI, dev-environment setup, non-standard stacks)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build LLM-powered workflows: MCP setup, agent skills, and prompt engineering tuned to each customer’s context&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn one-off solutions into reusable playbooks and product feedback, so patterns you solve once become self-serve or shipped product&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring&amp;nbsp; learnings on friction back to Figma&#39;s Product and Engineering teams, influence what gets built next, and often build it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;We&#39;d love to hear from you if you have:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years shipping production software end-to-end, with meaningful time embedded with customers or partner teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent customer-facing communication and technical partnership skills, with the ability to build trust with senior engineers and translate customer needs into actionable product and engineering solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong engineering fundamentals and adaptability, with the ability to quickly navigate unfamiliar codebases, languages, and technical environments to deliver production-ready solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with design systems and design-to-code workflows, including component libraries, tokens, documentation, and the tooling that connects design artifacts to production code&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in TypeScript/JavaScript or Python, including demonstrated fluency with agentic coding tools (e.g., MCP, agent orchestration). You have hands-on experience integrating APIs and SDKs, troubleshooting toolchains and CI environments, and navigating enterprise requirements such as SSO, security reviews, access controls, da

