&lt;p&gt;Product engineering at Descript means owning outcomes, not just tickets — you&#39;ll take a problem from a rough idea to a shipped, measured result, working closely with product, design, and the rest of engineering along the way. We organize around a few teams, each responsible for a distinct part of the product:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Editor:&lt;/strong&gt; owns our video editor. Help make traditionally complex video-editing workflows simpler, craft cutting-edge AI into practical creative tools, and build on our vision of turning a text-editor for video into a tool that puts video in everyone&#39;s communication toolkit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Growth &amp;amp; Monetization:&lt;/strong&gt; owns onboarding and activation, growth loops and in-product experiments, plans and pricing, checkout, billing, and AI credits. Help turn visitors into customers and customers into revenue.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Media:&lt;/strong&gt; owns upload, transcription, diarization, alignment, drive-wide search, playback, rendering, and export (including the engine we&#39;re rewriting in Rust 🦀). Help make media fast to bring in, easy to find, instant to play, and reliable to export.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Agent:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;owns Underlord, Descript’s AI co-editor. Build the representations, tools, harness, evals, and feedback loops that let it reason about video projects, make edits, and check its work. Help people and agents collaborate naturally, whether in the editor or through our API and MCP.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Identity &amp;amp; Access (aka TACO):&lt;/strong&gt; owns login, authentication and authorization, account settings, and project organization, plus the enterprise layer of workspaces, SSO/SCIM, governance, and audit logs. Help individuals become teams, and teams scale into enterprises, with the trust and security to go all in.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Regardless of your team you’ll have the opportunity to design thoughtful full-stack systems that work reliably and deliver value to new and existing users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own meaningful product surfaces end to end.&lt;/strong&gt; Take problems from definition through design, implementation, launch, measurement, and maintenance. Improve core Editor workflows, shape the self-serve journey from signup through renewal, or help make Underlord more sentient.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shape the product, not just the implementation.&lt;/strong&gt; Partner with Product and Design to propose better interactions, expose constraints, choose the right metrics, and find simpler paths to user outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build ambitious full-stack systems with care.&lt;/strong&gt; Create responsive, reliable experiences. Stretch from TypeScript and React to NodeJS and Temporal to first and third party integrations to get the job done.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Improve how the team learns and ships.&lt;/strong&gt; Form hypotheses, instrument your work, release incrementally, and read results honestly. Strengthen the tooling, standards, tests, observability, and release practices that help the team move quickly without compromising quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Raise the team’s technical ambition.&lt;/strong&gt; Provide architectural direction, thoughtful reviews, mentoring, and clear human writing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;What You Bring&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have 5+ years of experience building and shipping customer-facing products, including end-to-end features that measurably improved user or business outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You effectively leverage agents to multiply your impact and think critically about how to better harness AI in your work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ve owned features/experiments end to end, from planning through launch, and leveraged analytics and metrics to evaluate impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You orient quickly in unfamiliar systems by exploring and asking thoughtful questions to both your teammates and agents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You care about how software feels and notice when the technically correct result is still wrong for the user.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You create clarity in ambiguous work and can navigate (and simplify!) significant product and technical complexity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You validate your work rigorously through focused reproductions, logs, tests, and other evidence rather than trusting that the output looks right.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
